IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tas-interpretation-time`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1931 (Tasmania), ss 32 to 38: alternative procedure, attempts, corporations, similar crimes and offences, penalties, summary proceedings and indictment.
-- Answers of a rule of reading: JUST TRUE where the text applies to the case; JUST FALSE only where the text itself says no to the case in its own words
--   (a "means" definition, a condition introduced with "if", "only if", "as long as" or "unless", a list closed with "only", a flat negative, a "where" that fails, a period the text fixes and the case falls outside it);
-- NOTHING everywhere else (an open list, "includes", a term left undefined, silence, a pointer outside the sources, a grant or prohibition limited by its own wording where the case falls outside the limit, a scope limit with no "only").
-- A rule that returns a day, a name or a value has no second not-covered answer, so it returns NOTHING when its text does not apply.
-- A penalty is carried as a number whose unit is whatever the Act that specifies it uses; the Act itself gives no unit and no value for a penalty unit (see NOTES.md).
-- s 33 is shown only as a row of dots and is not encoded.

§ `s 32: alternative procedure in respect of offences`

-- src:671 | 32. Alternative procedure in respect of offences
-- src:673 | Except as otherwise provided by the Criminal Code Act 1924, where an act or omission constitutes an offence under each of 2 or more Acts or both under an Act and at common law, the offender shall be liable to be prosecuted and punished under either or any of such Acts or at common law, but shall not be liable to be punished twice for the same offence.
@ref s 32 liable to be prosecuted and punished (src:671-673)
GIVEN `the Criminal Code Act 1924 provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an act or omission constitutes an offence under each of 2 or more Acts, or both under an Act and at common law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 32: the offender is liable to be prosecuted and punished under either or any of those Acts or at common law` `the Criminal Code Act 1924 provides otherwise` `an act or omission constitutes an offence under each of 2 or more Acts, or both under an Act and at common law` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`an act or omission constitutes an offence under each of 2 or more Acts, or both under an Act and at common law`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "where"
           IF `the Criminal Code Act 1924 provides otherwise` THEN JUST FALSE   -- "Except as otherwise provided" met
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:671 | 32. Alternative procedure in respect of offences
-- src:673 | Except as otherwise provided by the Criminal Code Act 1924, where an act or omission constitutes an offence under each of 2 or more Acts or both under an Act and at common law, the offender shall be liable to be prosecuted and punished under either or any of such Acts or at common law, but shall not be liable to be punished twice for the same offence.
@ref s 32 not punished twice (src:671-673)
GIVEN `the Criminal Code Act 1924 provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an act or omission constitutes an offence under each of 2 or more Acts, or both under an Act and at common law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender has already been punished for the same offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 32: the offender is not liable to be punished twice for the same offence` `the Criminal Code Act 1924 provides otherwise` `an act or omission constitutes an offence under each of 2 or more Acts, or both under an Act and at common law` `the offender has already been punished for the same offence` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`an act or omission constitutes an offence under each of 2 or more Acts, or both under an Act and at common law`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "where"
           IF `the Criminal Code Act 1924 provides otherwise` THEN JUST FALSE   -- "Except as otherwise provided" met
           IF `the offender has already been punished for the same offence` THEN JUST TRUE   -- the text's "shall not be liable to be punished twice"
           OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- nothing yet to bar

#ASSERT `s 32: the offender is liable to be prosecuted and punished under either or any of those Acts or at common law` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 32: the offender is liable to be prosecuted and punished under either or any of those Acts or at common law` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 32: the offender is liable to be prosecuted and punished under either or any of those Acts or at common law` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 32: the offender is not liable to be punished twice for the same offence` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 32: the offender is not liable to be punished twice for the same offence` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 32: the offender is not liable to be punished twice for the same offence` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 32: the offender is not liable to be punished twice for the same offence` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 34: attempt to commit any offence to be an offence`

DECLARE `Penalty` HAS
    `the fine not exceeding` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the imprisonment not exceeding` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

-- src:679 | 34. Attempt to commit any offence to be an offence
-- src:681 | Where by any Act an offence is constituted, any attempt to commit such offence shall be an offence and be punishable in the same manner as the offence constituted by such Act.
@ref s 34 an offence (src:679-681)
GIVEN `by an Act an offence is constituted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person attempts to commit the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34: the attempt is an offence` `by an Act an offence is constituted` `the person attempts to commit the offence` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`by an Act an offence is constituted`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF NOT (`the person attempts to commit the offence`) THEN NOTHING   -- a scope limit with no "only"
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:679 | 34. Attempt to commit any offence to be an offence
-- src:681 | Where by any Act an offence is constituted, any attempt to commit such offence shall be an offence and be punishable in the same manner as the offence constituted by such Act.
@ref s 34 punishable in the same manner (src:679-681)
GIVEN `by an Act an offence is constituted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person attempts to commit the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the penalty for the offence constituted by the Act` IS A `Penalty`
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Penalty`)
`s 34: the attempt is punishable in the same manner as the offence, by the penalty` `by an Act an offence is constituted` `the person attempts to commit the offence` `the penalty for the offence constituted by the Act` MEANS
    IF `by an Act an offence is constituted` AND `the person attempts to commit the offence`
    THEN JUST `the penalty for the offence constituted by the Act`
    ELSE NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 34: the attempt is an offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 34: the attempt is an offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 34: the attempt is an offence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 34: the attempt is punishable in the same manner as the offence, by the penalty` TRUE TRUE (`Penalty` OF (JUST 500), (JUST 6)) EQUALS JUST (`Penalty` OF (JUST 500), (JUST 6))
#ASSERT `s 34: the attempt is punishable in the same manner as the offence, by the penalty` TRUE FALSE (`Penalty` OF (JUST 500), (JUST 6)) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 35: corporations`

DECLARE `Kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `an individual person`
    `a body corporate`

-- src:685 | (1) Every provision of an Act relating to offences punishable upon indictment or upon summary conviction shall be construed to apply to bodies corporate as well as to individual persons.
@ref s 35(1) (src:685)
GIVEN `the provision of an Act relates to offences punishable upon indictment or upon summary conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `Kind of person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35(1): the provision is construed to apply to the person` `the provision of an Act relates to offences punishable upon indictment or upon summary conviction` person MEANS
    IF `the provision of an Act relates to offences punishable upon indictment or upon summary conviction` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:687 | (2) Where under any Act any forfeiture or penalty is payable to a party aggrieved, it shall be payable to a body corporate where such body is the party aggrieved.
@ref s 35(2) (src:687)
GIVEN `under an Act a forfeiture or penalty is payable to a party aggrieved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party aggrieved is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35(2): the forfeiture or penalty is payable to the body corporate` `under an Act a forfeiture or penalty is payable to a party aggrieved` `the party aggrieved is a body corporate` MEANS
    IF `under an Act a forfeiture or penalty is payable to a party aggrieved` AND `the party aggrieved is a body corporate` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where" or a failed "where"

#ASSERT `s 35(1): the provision is construed to apply to the person` TRUE `an individual person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 35(1): the provision is construed to apply to the person` TRUE `a body corporate` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 35(1): the provision is construed to apply to the person` FALSE `a body corporate` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 35(2): the forfeiture or penalty is payable to the body corporate` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 35(2): the forfeiture or penalty is payable to the body corporate` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 35(2): the forfeiture or penalty is payable to the body corporate` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 36: crimes and offences where similar to be similarly dealt with`

-- src:691 | (1) Where an act or omission constitutes a crime under the provisions of any Act and the like act or omission constitutes an offence punishable summarily under the provisions of some other Act, the principles of criminal responsibility applicable in relation to such crime shall be applied in relation to such offence, and all terms and expressions used in relation to such offence shall have the same meaning and construction as when similarly used in relation to such crime.
@ref s 36(1) (src:691)
GIVEN `an act or omission constitutes a crime under the provisions of an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the like act or omission constitutes an offence punishable summarily under the provisions of some other Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 36(1): the principles of criminal responsibility applicable to the crime apply to the offence, and the terms and expressions used for the offence have the same meaning and construction as for the crime` `an act or omission constitutes a crime under the provisions of an Act` `the like act or omission constitutes an offence punishable summarily under the provisions of some other Act` MEANS
    IF `an act or omission constitutes a crime under the provisions of an Act` AND `the like act or omission constitutes an offence punishable summarily under the provisions of some other Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"

-- src:693 | (2) In any such case as aforesaid, the provisions of the Criminal Code, so far as the same are applicable and to the extent hereinbefore provided, shall be applied in relation to any such offence.
@ref s 36(2) (src:693)
GIVEN `section 36(1) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision of the Criminal Code is applicable to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 36(2): the provision of the Criminal Code applies in relation to the offence` `section 36(1) applies` `the provision of the Criminal Code is applicable to the offence` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`section 36(1) applies`) THEN NOTHING   -- "In any such case as aforesaid": a scope limit with no "only"
           IF `the provision of the Criminal Code is applicable to the offence` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- "so far as the same are applicable"

#ASSERT `s 36(1): the principles of criminal responsibility applicable to the crime apply to the offence, and the terms and expressions used for the offence have the same meaning and construction as for the crime` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 36(1): the principles of criminal responsibility applicable to the crime apply to the offence, and the terms and expressions used for the offence have the same meaning and construction as for the crime` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 36(1): the principles of criminal responsibility applicable to the crime apply to the offence, and the terms and expressions used for the offence have the same meaning and construction as for the crime` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 36(2): the provision of the Criminal Code applies in relation to the offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 36(2): the provision of the Criminal Code applies in relation to the offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 36(2): the provision of the Criminal Code applies in relation to the offence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 37: effect of specifying penalties in Acts`

-- src:697 | (1) Where in an Act a penalty is specified in respect of a contravention of, or a failure to comply with, that Act or a provision of that Act, then, unless the contrary is expressly provided, that specification indicates that the contravention or failure to comply is an offence punishable by a penalty not exceeding that so specified.
@ref s 37(1) (src:697)
GIVEN `in an Act a penalty is specified in respect of a contravention of, or a failure to comply with, that Act or a provision of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is expressly provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 37(1): the contravention or failure to comply is an offence punishable by a penalty not exceeding the one specified` `in an Act a penalty is specified in respect of a contravention of, or a failure to comply with, that Act or a provision of that Act` `the contrary is expressly provided` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`in an Act a penalty is specified in respect of a contravention of, or a failure to comply with, that Act or a provision of that Act`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF `the contrary is expressly provided` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:699 | (2) Where in an Act a penalty is specified in respect of an offence against that Act, or a provision of that Act, then, unless the contrary is expressly provided, that specification indicates that the offence is punishable by a penalty not exceeding that so specified.
@ref s 37(2) (src:699)
GIVEN `in an Act a penalty is specified in respect of an offence against that Act, or a provision of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is expressly provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 37(2): the offence is punishable by a penalty not exceeding the one specified` `in an Act a penalty is specified in respect of an offence against that Act, or a provision of that Act` `the contrary is expressly provided` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`in an Act a penalty is specified in respect of an offence against that Act, or a provision of that Act`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF `the contrary is expressly provided` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `Place where a penalty is specified` IS ONE OF
    `at the foot of a section, without qualification`
    `at the foot of a subsection of a section, but not at the foot of the section`
    `at the foot of a section, expressed to apply to a specified subsection or specified subsections`

DECLARE `Provision whose contravention is an offence` IS ONE OF
    `the section`
    `the subsection at whose foot the penalty is specified`
    `any of the specified subsections`

-- src:701 | (3) Where in an Act a penalty –
-- src:703 | (a) is specified without qualification at the foot of a section of an Act;
-- src:705 | (b) is specified at the foot of a subsection of a section of the Act, but not at the foot of the section; or
-- src:707 | (c) is specified at the foot of a section of the Act and expressed to apply to a specified subsection or specified subsections of the section –
-- src:709 | then, unless the contrary is expressly provided, that specification indicates that a contravention of, or failure to comply with, the section or subsection, or, as the case may be, any of the subsections, is an offence and that the offence is punishable by a penalty not exceeding that so specified.
@ref s 37(3) (src:701-709)
GIVEN place IS A `Place where a penalty is specified`
      `the contrary is expressly provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Provision whose contravention is an offence`)
`s 37(3): a contravention of, or failure to comply with, the provision is an offence punishable by a penalty not exceeding the one specified, the provision being` place `the contrary is expressly provided` MEANS
    IF `the contrary is expressly provided`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER place
        WHEN `at the foot of a section, without qualification` THEN JUST `the section`
        WHEN `at the foot of a subsection of a section, but not at the foot of the section` THEN JUST `the subsection at whose foot the penalty is specified`
        WHEN `at the foot of a section, expressed to apply to a specified subsection or specified subsections` THEN JUST `any of the specified subsections`

-- src:711 | (4) Where in an Act a maximum penalty and a minimum penalty are specified in respect of an offence against the Act or a provision of the Act, that specification indicates that the offence is punishable by a penalty not less than that minimum nor greater than that maximum.
@ref s 37(4) (src:711)
GIVEN `the minimum penalty specified` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum penalty specified` IS A NUMBER
      `the penalty imposed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 37(4): the penalty imposed is one the offence is punishable by` `the minimum penalty specified` `the maximum penalty specified` `the penalty imposed` MEANS
    `the penalty imposed` AT LEAST `the minimum penalty specified` AND `the penalty imposed` AT MOST `the maximum penalty specified`

-- src:713 | (5) Where in an Act a penalty or a fine specified in respect of an offence against the Act, or a provision of the Act, is referred to as being a daily penalty or a daily fine, that reference indicates that a penalty or a fine not exceeding that daily penalty or daily fine may, in addition to any other penalty or fine that may be imposed in respect of the offence, be imposed for each day or part of a day during which the offence continues.
@ref s 37(5) (src:713)
GIVEN `the daily penalty or daily fine specified` IS A NUMBER
      `the first day on which the offence continues` IS A DATE
      `the last day on which the offence continues` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 37(5): the most that may be imposed for the continuing offence, in addition to any other penalty or fine` `the daily penalty or daily fine specified` `the first day on which the offence continues` `the last day on which the offence continues` MEANS
    `the daily penalty or daily fine specified` TIMES (((`the last day on which the offence continues`) MINUS (`the first day on which the offence continues`)) PLUS 1)

DECLARE `Way an offence is punishable` IS ONE OF
    `by the fine`
    `by the term of imprisonment`
    `by both the fine and the term of imprisonment`

-- src:715 | (5A) Where in an Act a penalty specified in respect of an offence against the Act or a provision of the Act is a fine or term of imprisonment, the offence is, unless the contrary is expressly provided, punishable by the fine, or by the term of imprisonment, or both.
@ref s 37(5A) (src:715)
GIVEN `the penalty specified is a fine or term of imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is expressly provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      way IS A `Way an offence is punishable`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 37(5A): the offence is punishable` `the penalty specified is a fine or term of imprisonment` `the contrary is expressly provided` way MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the penalty specified is a fine or term of imprisonment`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF `the contrary is expressly provided` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:717 | (6) Nothing in the Penalty Units and Other Penalties Act 1987 affects or prejudices the application of this section in respect of the specification of a penalty in an Act, whether or not that penalty was so specified before, or that penalty is so specified on or after, the day on which the Penalty Units and Other Penalties Act 1987 receives the Royal Assent.
@ref s 37(6) (src:717)
GIVEN `the matter is the specification of a penalty in an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 37(6): the Penalty Units and Other Penalties Act 1987 does not affect or prejudice the application of section 37` `the matter is the specification of a penalty in an Act` MEANS
    IF `the matter is the specification of a penalty in an Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- a scope limit with no "only"

