§ `s 38: summary proceedings, proceedings by indictment and the like`

DECLARE `Way proceedings are taken` IS ONE OF
    `summarily, in accordance with the Justices Act 1959`
    `by indictment, in accordance with the provisions of the Criminal Code`

-- Section 38(1) and section 38(2) can both apply to one offence that is punishable on indictment and also punishable on summary conviction.
-- The text does not say which prevails, so the answer is then NOTHING.
-- src:729 | (2) Where a provision of an Act –
-- src:731 | (a) constitutes a crime;
-- src:733 | (b) makes an offence punishable on indictment; or
-- src:735 | (c) makes an offence punishable by imprisonment for a term exceeding 3 years without specifying or indicating that the offence is to be dealt with summarily –
-- src:737 | proceedings in respect of the crime or offence shall be by indictment in accordance with the provisions of the Criminal Code.
@ref s 38(2) (src:729-737)
GIVEN `the provision constitutes a crime` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision makes an offence punishable on indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term of imprisonment the provision makes an offence punishable by` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the provision specifies or indicates that the offence is to be dealt with summarily` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38(2): the proceedings in respect of the crime or offence are by indictment` `the provision constitutes a crime` `the provision makes an offence punishable on indictment` `the term of imprisonment the provision makes an offence punishable by` `the provision specifies or indicates that the offence is to be dealt with summarily` MEANS
    `the provision constitutes a crime`
    OR `the provision makes an offence punishable on indictment`
    OR (CONSIDER `the term of imprisonment the provision makes an offence punishable by`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST years THEN `s 38(2)(c): a term of imprisonment exceeds 3 years` years AND NOT (`the provision specifies or indicates that the offence is to be dealt with summarily`))

-- src:721 | (1) Where a provision of an Act expressly or by implication provides –
-- src:723 | (a) that any matter or proceeding is to be heard and determined, or dealt with, summarily or by or before justices or a court of summary jurisdiction; or
-- src:725 | (b) that an offence is punishable on summary conviction or that a person is liable on summary conviction to a specified penalty or to a penalty not exceeding a specified penalty –
-- src:727 | the matter or proceeding shall be heard and determined, or shall be dealt with, or, as the case may be, the proceedings in respect of the offence shall be taken, in accordance with the Justices Act 1959, and any penalty imposed in respect of the matter, proceeding, or offence may be enforced and recovered as provided by the Sentencing Act 1997.
-- src:729 | (2) Where a provision of an Act –
-- src:731 | (a) constitutes a crime;
-- src:733 | (b) makes an offence punishable on indictment; or
-- src:735 | (c) makes an offence punishable by imprisonment for a term exceeding 3 years without specifying or indicating that the offence is to be dealt with summarily –
-- src:737 | proceedings in respect of the crime or offence shall be by indictment in accordance with the provisions of the Criminal Code.
-- src:739 | (3) Subject to subsection (2), where –
-- src:741 | (a) by a provision of an Act an offence not declared expressly or by implication to be a crime is constituted or made punishable, or any penalty or forfeiture may be imposed in respect of any matter; and
-- src:743 | (b) that Act does not contain provisions relating to the manner in which proceedings in respect of the offence shall be taken, or the matter shall be heard and determined –
-- src:745 | the proceedings in respect of the offence shall be taken, or, as the case may be, the matter shall be heard and determined, in accordance with the Justices Act 1959, and any penalty or forfeiture which may be imposed in respect of the offence or matter may be enforced and recovered as provided by that Act.
@ref s 38 dispatcher (src:721-745)
GIVEN `a provision of an Act expressly or by implication provides that the matter or proceeding is to be dealt with summarily, or that the offence is punishable on summary conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are by indictment under section 38(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by a provision of the Act an offence not declared expressly or by implication to be a crime is constituted or made punishable, or a penalty or forfeiture may be imposed in respect of a matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act contains provisions relating to the manner in which proceedings shall be taken or the matter heard and determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Way proceedings are taken`)
`s 38: the proceedings are taken` `a provision of an Act expressly or by implication provides that the matter or proceeding is to be dealt with summarily, or that the offence is punishable on summary conviction` `the proceedings are by indictment under section 38(2)` `by a provision of the Act an offence not declared expressly or by implication to be a crime is constituted or made punishable, or a penalty or forfeiture may be imposed in respect of a matter` `the Act contains provisions relating to the manner in which proceedings shall be taken or the matter heard and determined` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `a provision of an Act expressly or by implication provides that the matter or proceeding is to be dealt with summarily, or that the offence is punishable on summary conviction` AND `the proceedings are by indictment under section 38(2)` THEN NOTHING
           IF `the proceedings are by indictment under section 38(2)` THEN JUST `by indictment, in accordance with the provisions of the Criminal Code`
           IF `a provision of an Act expressly or by implication provides that the matter or proceeding is to be dealt with summarily, or that the offence is punishable on summary conviction` THEN JUST `summarily, in accordance with the Justices Act 1959`
           IF `by a provision of the Act an offence not declared expressly or by implication to be a crime is constituted or made punishable, or a penalty or forfeiture may be imposed in respect of a matter` AND NOT (`the Act contains provisions relating to the manner in which proceedings shall be taken or the matter heard and determined`) THEN JUST `summarily, in accordance with the Justices Act 1959`
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- The Act under which a penalty is enforced and recovered: section 38(1) names the Sentencing Act 1997, and section 38(3) names the Justices Act 1959.
-- src:721 | (1) Where a provision of an Act expressly or by implication provides –
-- src:723 | (a) that any matter or proceeding is to be heard and determined, or dealt with, summarily or by or before justices or a court of summary jurisdiction; or
-- src:725 | (b) that an offence is punishable on summary conviction or that a person is liable on summary conviction to a specified penalty or to a penalty not exceeding a specified penalty –
-- src:727 | the matter or proceeding shall be heard and determined, or shall be dealt with, or, as the case may be, the proceedings in respect of the offence shall be taken, in accordance with the Justices Act 1959, and any penalty imposed in respect of the matter, proceeding, or offence may be enforced and recovered as provided by the Sentencing Act 1997.
-- src:739 | (3) Subject to subsection (2), where –
-- src:741 | (a) by a provision of an Act an offence not declared expressly or by implication to be a crime is constituted or made punishable, or any penalty or forfeiture may be imposed in respect of any matter; and
-- src:743 | (b) that Act does not contain provisions relating to the manner in which proceedings in respect of the offence shall be taken, or the matter shall be heard and determined –
-- src:745 | the proceedings in respect of the offence shall be taken, or, as the case may be, the matter shall be heard and determined, in accordance with the Justices Act 1959, and any penalty or forfeiture which may be imposed in respect of the offence or matter may be enforced and recovered as provided by that Act.
@ref s 38 enforcement (src:721-727) (src:739-745)
GIVEN `section 38(1) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 38(3) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 38: the penalty or forfeiture may be enforced and recovered as provided by` `section 38(1) applies` `section 38(3) applies` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `section 38(1) applies` THEN JUST "the Sentencing Act 1997"
           IF `section 38(3) applies` THEN JUST "the Justices Act 1959"
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:747 | (4) Where a provision of an Act provides that an infringement notice may be issued for an offence, any such infringement notice is to be dealt with in accordance with the Monetary Penalties Enforcement Act 2005.
@ref s 38(4) (src:747)
GIVEN `a provision of an Act provides that an infringement notice may be issued for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 38(4): the infringement notice is to be dealt with in accordance with` `a provision of an Act provides that an infringement notice may be issued for an offence` MEANS
    IF `a provision of an Act provides that an infringement notice may be issued for an offence` THEN JUST "the Monetary Penalties Enforcement Act 2005" ELSE NOTHING

